  "content": {
    "id": "p50-q25-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "Erin goes off on a long bike ride, averaging 10 km/h.\nOne hour later her brother Alistair starts chasing after her at 16 km/h.\nHow long will it take Alistair to catch up to Erin?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "1 hour 40 minutes after Alistair starts.",
      "worked": "Let $t$ be the time in hours after Alistair starts and $d$ the distance travelled from their starting point in kilometres.\n\nErin has a one-hour head start:\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=10(t+1) &&(1)\\\\d&=16t &&(2)\\end{align*}$$\nEquating the distances:\n$$\\begin{align*}10(t+1)&=16t\\\\10t+10&=16t\\\\6t&=10\\\\t&=\\frac{5}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nAlistair catches Erin 1 hour 40 minutes after he starts.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
